1. <p>Launch a local IaaS-style instance for a fictional kirana chain's order portal: create a linked clone of 'lab_server01' from its 'clean_base' snapshot named 'cloud_instance01' with `VBoxManage clonevm lab_server01 --snapshot clean_base --options link --name cloud_instance01 --register`, set 1 vCPU and 768 MB RAM with `VBoxManage modifyvm`, and start it. Constraint: Keep 'lab_server01' and 'lab_client01' powered off while it runs.</p>
=>VBoxManage clonevm lab_server01 --snapshot clean_base --options link --name cloud_instance01 --register
VBoxManage modifyvm cloud_instance01 --cpus 1 --memory 768
VBoxManage controlvm lab_server01 poweroff   # ensure both source VMs stay off
VBoxManage controlvm lab_client01 poweroff
VBoxManage startvm cloud_instance01

2. <p>Deploy a static page on 'cloud_instance01': create '/srv/kirana_site/index.html' with the heading 'Kirana Bazaar Order Status' and three fictional order IDs, serve it with `python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory /srv/kirana_site`, and open it from your laptop browser at the instance's host-only IP. Hint: Create the folder with `sudo mkdir -p` and `sudo chown labadmin`, and keep the server running in a second SSH session.</p>
=>ssh labadmin@<cloud_instance01-ip>
sudo mkdir -p /srv/kirana_site
sudo chown labadmin /srv/kirana_site
cat > /srv/kirana_site/index.html <<'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><title>Kirana Bazaar Order Status</title></head>
<body>
<h1>Kirana Bazaar Order Status</h1>
<ul>
  <li>Order #KB-1001 — Dispatched</li>
  <li>Order #KB-1002 — Packed</li>
  <li>Order #KB-1003 — Delivered</li>
</ul>
</body></html>
EOF

3 <p>Estimate the monthly cost of the smallest general-purpose Linux instance with at least 1 GB RAM, running 24x7 in an India region, using the public pricing calculators of AWS, Azure and Google Cloud. Save 'aws_estimate.png', 'azure_estimate.png', 'gcp_estimate.png' and a 'cloud_cost_comparison.txt' with one line per provider: instance type and monthly estimate. Constraint: Do not sign in, create an account or start a trial.</p>
