4. <p>Finish by proving the instance lifecycle from your laptop: `curl -i --max-time 5 http://<instance IP>:8080/` must return 200, power off 'cloud_instance01' and the same command must fail, then start it, restart the page server and the command must return 200 again. Save all three outputs and `VBoxManage list vms` in 'cloud_basics_proof.txt' and submit it with the earlier files.</p>
=>{
  echo "=== curl while instance is UP ==="
  curl -i --max-time 5 http://<cloud_instance01-ip>:8080/

  VBoxManage controlvm cloud_instance01 poweroff

  echo "=== curl while instance is OFF (expect failure/timeout) ==="
  curl -i --max-time 5 http://<cloud_instance01-ip>:8080/

  VBoxManage startvm cloud_instance01
  # SSH back in and restart: cd /srv/kirana_site && python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory /srv/kirana_site &

  echo "=== curl after restart (expect 200 again) ==="
  curl -i --max-time 5 http://<cloud_instance01-ip>:8080/

  echo "=== VBoxManage list vms ==="
  VBoxManage list vms
} > cloud_basics_proof.txt
